                <pb facs="0531" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sperry to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 60.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I have
                    received from the minister for foreign affairs a communication in regard to the
                    taxation of foreigners, resident here, who are engaged in trade. This
                    communication was received at this legation about ten days after the Persian
                    date of it. A copy of this communication is herewith inclosed, with the
                    translation. I have forwarded copies of this communication to each of the
                    several groups of American citizens residing in Persia, with an explanatory
                    note, a copy of which is inclosed. It is only in regard to their medical
                    operations that the American missionaries could be brought under the terms of
                    this new order. As both medical services and drugs are furnished by them without
                    cost in those cases where the patient is unable to pay, I am of the opinion that
                    they will not be held by the Persian Government to be engaged in trade, within
                    the meaning of the new order.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Watson R. Sperry.</hi></signed></closer>



